# Database and API

- Use explicit, versioned migrations; never depend on undocumented manual database edits.
- Add indexes based on known query patterns and verify expensive query plans when relevant.
- Prevent N+1 queries and unbounded collection endpoints; paginate large result sets.
- Define stable API error formats and meaningful status codes.
- Validate inputs and authorize every operation server-side.
- Enforce channel/account ownership and tenant boundaries in application or data-access logic.
- Use transactions for related writes that must remain consistent.
- Use idempotency keys for external publishing actions where supported.
- Never expose secrets, OAuth tokens, or provider credentials to the browser.
- Add migration, repository, authorization, and API tests for meaningful changes.
